Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.64,0:00:23.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎收看《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:00:22.64,0:00:23.60,Original,,0,0,0,,On how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.36,0:00:25.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,复印纸
Dialogue: 1,0:00:25.36,0:00:25.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Copy paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.72,0:00:29.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑本应让办公室实现无纸化
Dialogue: 1,0:00:26.72,0:00:29.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Computers were supposed to make our offices paperless.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.84,0:00:32.62,Translation,,0,0,0,,然而，这些预言大错特错
Dialogue: 1,0:00:29.84,0:00:32.62,Original,,0,0,0,,However, those predictions couldn't have been more wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.44,0:00:41.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,牛仔裤。刚问世时，除了工厂工人，没人愿意穿它
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.44,0:00:41.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Jeans. When they were first invented, nobody would be caught dead in them, except the factory workers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.56,0:00:44.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,但后来猫王和詹姆斯·迪恩穿上了它
Dialogue: 1,0:00:42.56,0:00:44.88,Original,,0,0,0,,But along came Elvis and James Dean.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.68,0:00:48.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑
Dialogue: 1,0:00:47.68,0:00:48.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Computers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.20,0:00:51.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,30 年前，没人知道这是什么
Dialogue: 1,0:00:49.20,0:00:51.52,Original,,0,0,0,,30 years ago, nobody would have known what this was.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.16,0:00:53.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今，我们已离不开它
Dialogue: 1,0:00:52.16,0:00:53.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Today, we couldn't live without one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.48,0:00:57.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今从零组装一台只需 90 分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:00:54.48,0:00:57.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Now it takes just 90 minutes to assemble one from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.28,0:01:00.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有平板玻璃
Dialogue: 1,0:00:59.28,0:01:00.00,Original,,0,0,0,,And plate glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.96,0:01:02.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,它的历史超过 4000 年
Dialogue: 1,0:01:00.96,0:01:02.88,Original,,0,0,0,,It's been around for over 4,000 years,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.44,0:01:07.46,Translation,,0,0,0,,但自罗马时代以来，其制造工艺几乎没变
Dialogue: 1,0:01:03.44,0:01:07.46,Original,,0,0,0,,but its construction has remained pretty much the same since the time of the Romans.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.36,0:01:09.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先
Dialogue: 1,0:01:09.36,0:01:09.92,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.44,0:01:16.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑曾被预言会把纸张送回石器时代
Dialogue: 1,0:01:13.44,0:01:16.72,Original,,0,0,0,,computers were supposed to send paper back to the Stone Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.60,0:01:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,无纸化办公室似乎指日可待
Dialogue: 1,0:01:17.60,0:01:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The paperless office was supposed to be just around the corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.56,0:01:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,不再有信件，只有电子邮件
Dialogue: 1,0:01:20.56,0:01:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,With no more letters, just emails.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.44,0:01:25.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,然而，这些预言全都落空
Dialogue: 1,0:01:23.44,0:01:25.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Well, those predictions were wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.68,0:01:29.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,复印机和打印机反而让用纸量空前增加
Dialogue: 1,0:01:25.68,0:01:29.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Photocopiers and printers have us using more paper than ever before.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.80,0:01:37.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,造纸始于原木运抵工厂
Dialogue: 1,0:01:34.80,0:01:37.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Paper production begins with the arrival of wood at the mill.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.56,0:01:45.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种纸由纸浆制成，纸浆来自 65% 枫木、25% 桦木和 10% 杨木
Dialogue: 1,0:01:38.56,0:01:45.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This paper is made from a paste produced from a mix of 65% maple, 25% birch, and 10% poplar.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.40,0:01:50.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,生产 1 吨纸浆需要 2 吨木材
Dialogue: 1,0:01:46.40,0:01:50.00,Original,,0,0,0,,It requires 2 tons of wood to produce 1 ton of paste.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.64,0:01:52.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,一切从这台剥皮滚筒开始
Dialogue: 1,0:01:50.64,0:01:52.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Everything starts from this debarking drum,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.96,0:01:54.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,它负责去除原木的树皮
Dialogue: 1,0:01:52.96,0:01:54.64,Original,,0,0,0,,which removes bark from the logs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.20,0:01:56.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,整个过程约 20 分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:01:55.20,0:01:56.88,Original,,0,0,0,,It's about a 20-minute operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.60,0:02:01.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,树皮将被燃烧，为工厂运转提供所需蒸汽
Dialogue: 1,0:01:57.60,0:02:01.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The bark will be burned to produce steam required for the operation of the mill.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.04,0:02:05.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,去皮的原木由这条传送带运送
Dialogue: 1,0:02:03.04,0:02:05.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The stripped logs are transported on this conveyor.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.68,0:02:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着原木被切成小块，称为木片
Dialogue: 1,0:02:19.68,0:02:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the logs are reduced into small pieces called kindling.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.60,0:02:27.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,木片堆成堆露天存放，无论冬夏
Dialogue: 1,0:02:23.60,0:02:27.36,Original,,0,0,0,,They're accumulated into a pile and remain outdoors, winter and summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.56,0:02:34.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这 5 堆木片共约 3 万吨
Dialogue: 1,0:02:30.56,0:02:34.00,Original,,0,0,0,,These 5 piles total about 30,000 tons of kindling.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.80,0:02:37.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,下一步是把木片加工成纸浆
Dialogue: 1,0:02:34.80,0:02:37.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The next step is to reduce the kindling into paste.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.48,0:02:39.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,先要清洗木片
Dialogue: 1,0:02:38.48,0:02:39.60,Original,,0,0,0,,They begin by washing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.04,0:02:45.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块屏幕用于确认清洗机装载正确
Dialogue: 1,0:02:43.04,0:02:45.84,Original,,0,0,0,,This screen verifies that the washer is properly loaded.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.84,0:02:49.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是碱煮
Dialogue: 1,0:02:47.84,0:02:49.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Then comes alkaline cooking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.20,0:02:53.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台巨大的圆筒就是蒸煮器，木片在其中
Dialogue: 1,0:02:51.20,0:02:53.84,Original,,0,0,0,,This huge cylinder is the washer in which the kindling
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.84,0:02:58.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,以 158 摄氏度的温度蒸煮数小时
Dialogue: 1,0:02:53.84,0:02:58.64,Original,,0,0,0,,is cooked for several hours at a temperature of 158 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.92,0:03:01.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是回收锅炉
Dialogue: 1,0:02:59.92,0:03:01.92,Original,,0,0,0,,And this is the recuperation boiler.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.56,0:03:04.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,它以 1000 度的高温燃烧木材
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.56,0:03:04.80,Original,,0,0,0,,It burns wood at 1,000 degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.68,0:03:09.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,熔化后如熔岩般流出的化学物质可被回收
Dialogue: 1,0:03:05.68,0:03:09.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Certain chemical products which come out fused as lava are recuperated.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.40,0:03:14.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,黑液是燃烧木材的残渣，将用于燃烧产生蒸汽
Dialogue: 1,0:03:10.40,0:03:14.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This black liquor, a residue of burned wood, will be burned to produce steam.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.32,0:03:19.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,离开蒸煮器后，褐色纸浆经清洗送入增稠器
Dialogue: 1,0:03:16.32,0:03:19.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Exiting the washer, the brown paste is washed and sent to the thickener.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.36,0:03:25.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用这把刮刀检查褐色纸浆的清洗质量
Dialogue: 1,0:03:21.36,0:03:25.12,Original,,0,0,0,,With this spatula, they verify the quality of the brown paste's washing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.92,0:03:27.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸浆现在必须进行漂白
Dialogue: 1,0:03:25.92,0:03:27.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The paste must now be bleached.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.16,0:03:31.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台碱性萃取塔让褐色纸浆
Dialogue: 1,0:03:28.16,0:03:31.28,Original,,0,0,0,,This alkaline extraction tower places the brown paste
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.28,0:03:33.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,与化学药剂充分接触
Dialogue: 1,0:03:31.28,0:03:33.12,Original,,0,0,0,,in contact with chemical products.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.76,0:03:37.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,用二氧化氯漂白后，纸浆逐渐变白
Dialogue: 1,0:03:33.76,0:03:37.52,Original,,0,0,0,,It's bleached with chlorine dioxide and gradually becomes whiter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.40,0:03:40.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后脱除部分水分
Dialogue: 1,0:03:38.40,0:03:40.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the water is partially drawn off.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.32,0:03:46.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,螺旋输送器打散纸浆，以便泵入储浆池
Dialogue: 1,0:03:42.32,0:03:46.56,Original,,0,0,0,,This worm screw breaks up the paste so it can be pumped into storage reservoirs.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.04,0:03:51.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台设备负责脱水
Dialogue: 1,0:03:49.04,0:03:51.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Water is extracted with this equipment,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.36,0:03:53.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,即贝尔瓦德·贝尔贝 3 型造纸机
Dialogue: 1,0:03:51.36,0:03:53.76,Original,,0,0,0,,the Belwård Belbay 3 paper machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.08,0:03:59.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,从进纸到出纸，运行速度达每分钟 1060 米
Dialogue: 1,0:03:54.08,0:03:59.76,Original,,0,0,0,,operating at a speed of 1,060 meters a minute between the entry and the exit.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.16,0:04:04.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸浆含水量从 95% 降至 5%
Dialogue: 1,0:04:00.16,0:04:04.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The concentration of water in the paste falls from 95 to 5%.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.80,0:04:13.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里可以看到纸张从压榨机中出来
Dialogue: 1,0:04:10.80,0:04:13.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Here we see the sheet of paper coming out of the presses.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.12,0:04:19.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后分析仪检测纸张的质量参数并提示故障
Dialogue: 1,0:04:15.12,0:04:19.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Then analysers verify the quality parameters of the paper and signal any faults.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.44,0:04:26.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸张随后被卷起
Dialogue: 1,0:04:25.44,0:04:26.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The paper is then rolled up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.52,0:04:30.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台卷取辊生产巨大的主纸卷
Dialogue: 1,0:04:27.52,0:04:30.08,Original,,0,0,0,,This roller produces enormous main spools.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.84,0:04:39.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,用这台换卷臂把满卷换成空卷筒
Dialogue: 1,0:04:35.84,0:04:39.12,Original,,0,0,0,,With this transfer arm, they change a full spool for an empty one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.00,0:04:44.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,一卷纸重逾 35 吨，内含 60 公里长的纸
Dialogue: 1,0:04:40.00,0:04:44.32,Original,,0,0,0,,A roll weighs over 35 tonnes and contains 60 kilometres of paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.92,0:04:49.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,复卷机把主纸卷分切成较窄的小卷
Dialogue: 1,0:04:45.92,0:04:49.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The spooler cuts the main spools into smaller, less wide rolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.92,0:04:53.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,部分直接发货，其余运往纸张裁切厂
Dialogue: 1,0:04:49.92,0:04:53.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Some will be delivered as is, while others will be shipped to paper cutters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.72,0:05:04.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,纸卷送入自动化仓库
Dialogue: 1,0:05:02.72,0:05:04.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Rolls are sent to an automated warehouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.52,0:05:10.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,仓库中存放着待日后裁切的纸卷
Dialogue: 1,0:05:07.52,0:05:10.40,Original,,0,0,0,,In the warehouse, they store rolls which will be cut later.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.84,0:05:15.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器人沿着地面轨道运行
Dialogue: 1,0:05:13.84,0:05:15.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Robots, guided on rails in the floor,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.32,0:05:18.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,将纸卷送入贝洛马蒂克裁纸机
Dialogue: 1,0:05:16.32,0:05:18.00,Original,,0,0,0,,feed the belomatic paper cutter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.72,0:05:20.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器生产复印纸
Dialogue: 1,0:05:18.72,0:05:20.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This is one that produces copy paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.60,0:05:25.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器人由中央电脑控制，并接受操作员调度
Dialogue: 1,0:05:21.60,0:05:25.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Robots are controlled by a central computer, directed by operators.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.60,0:05:38.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,生产速度达每分钟 5.5 万张
Dialogue: 1,0:05:35.60,0:05:38.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Production reaches 55,000 sheets per minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.72,0:05:44.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,4 台自动接纸器和操作员在包装前检验纸张质量
Dialogue: 1,0:05:40.72,0:05:44.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Four automatic catchers and operators verify paper quality before packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.48,0:05:53.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,该厂每小时生产 6600 包复印纸
Dialogue: 1,0:05:48.48,0:05:53.36,Original,,0,0,0,,In 1 hour, this mill produces 6,600 packages of copy paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.20,0:06:08.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,牛仔裤刚发明时，没人愿意穿它
Dialogue: 1,0:06:05.20,0:06:08.40,Original,,0,0,0,,When they were first invented, nobody would be caught dead in them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.48,0:06:11.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,除了工厂工人、农民和工匠
Dialogue: 1,0:06:08.48,0:06:11.44,Original,,0,0,0,,except for factory workers, farmers, and tradesmen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.08,0:06:14.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,但猫王和詹姆斯·迪恩穿上之后
Dialogue: 1,0:06:12.08,0:06:14.08,Original,,0,0,0,,But when Elvis and James Dean wore them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.32,0:06:18.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们就此不朽，牛仔裤也进入了时尚界
Dialogue: 1,0:06:14.32,0:06:18.16,Original,,0,0,0,,they became immortal, and jeans entered into the world of fashion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.28,0:06:22.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今，它们已是世界上最受欢迎的服装之一
Dialogue: 1,0:06:19.28,0:06:22.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Today, they're one of the most popular clothing items in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.12,0:06:32.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,牛仔裤由一种极为结实的棉布制成，即牛仔布
Dialogue: 1,0:06:29.12,0:06:32.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Jeans are made from a highly rugged cotton called denim.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.36,0:06:42.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,这卷巨大的布料长 450 米，可制成 350 条牛仔裤
Dialogue: 1,0:06:35.36,0:06:42.32,Original,,0,0,0,,This enormous roll contains 450 meters of fabric, from which they'll produce 350 pairs of jeans.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.04,0:06:46.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,数层布料在这张长桌上展开
Dialogue: 1,0:06:43.04,0:06:46.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Several thicknesses of the material are unrolled on this long table.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.68,0:06:51.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,这把刀一次可裁切多达 100 层布料
Dialogue: 1,0:06:47.68,0:06:51.12,Original,,0,0,0,,This knife can cut up to 100 pieces of the material at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.68,0:06:55.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料层数越多，一刀裁下就能得到厚厚一摞裁片
Dialogue: 1,0:06:51.68,0:06:55.92,Original,,0,0,0,,By multiplying the thicknesses, they produce a whole pile of pieces with one cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.96,0:07:03.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们按照裁剪样板裁出牛仔布裁片
Dialogue: 1,0:07:00.96,0:07:03.76,Original,,0,0,0,,They shape the denim pieces following cutting patterns.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.32,0:07:06.86,Translation,,0,0,0,,牛仔裤的每个部位都有自己的样板
Dialogue: 1,0:07:04.32,0:07:06.86,Original,,0,0,0,,Each piece of the jean has its own cutting pattern.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.92,0:07:12.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,小块布料用冲裁机裁切
Dialogue: 1,0:07:09.92,0:07:12.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The little pieces of fabric are cut with a clicker,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.48,0:07:16.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,也叫冲压机，用模具冲出口袋
Dialogue: 1,0:07:12.48,0:07:16.08,Original,,0,0,0,,also known as a stamper, which cuts out pockets with a cutting mold.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.80,0:07:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,它施加巨大压力，一次可冲出 20 个口袋
Dialogue: 1,0:07:16.80,0:07:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Exerting immense pressure, it can cut 20 pockets at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.02,0:07:23.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,开始缝纫
Dialogue: 1,0:07:22.02,0:07:23.12,Original,,0,0,0,,They begin sewing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.76,0:07:26.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,牛仔裤用 100% 纯棉线缝制
Dialogue: 1,0:07:23.76,0:07:26.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Jeans are sewn with 100% cotton thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.88,0:07:30.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,机针每分钟刺入布料 4000 次
Dialogue: 1,0:07:26.88,0:07:30.08,Original,,0,0,0,,This needle pierces the fabric 4,000 times a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.64,0:07:39.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器在口袋上绣出图案
Dialogue: 1,0:07:36.64,0:07:39.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Designs are embroidered on the pockets with this machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.92,0:07:43.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,其机针每分钟运动 2500 次
Dialogue: 1,0:07:39.92,0:07:43.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Its needles move at 2,500 strokes per minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.12,0:07:53.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台口袋机器臂可同时完成折叠、压烫和缝合口袋
Dialogue: 1,0:07:49.12,0:07:53.28,Original,,0,0,0,,This pocket robot will simultaneously fold, press, and sew a pocket.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.00,0:07:58.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器 60 分钟可安装 75 个口袋
Dialogue: 1,0:07:54.00,0:07:58.56,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine allows for the installation of 75 pockets in 60 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.68,0:08:11.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,口袋现已缝合到位
Dialogue: 1,0:08:09.68,0:08:11.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The pocket is now sewn into place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.68,0:08:21.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,下一步是锁扣眼
Dialogue: 1,0:08:19.68,0:08:21.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The next step is the buttonhole.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.84,0:08:24.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器沿扣眼轮廓缝制
Dialogue: 1,0:08:21.84,0:08:24.24,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine sews the contours of the buttonhole,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.40,0:08:26.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后一把钢刀落下，切开开口
Dialogue: 1,0:08:24.40,0:08:26.96,Original,,0,0,0,,and a steel blade comes down to cut the opening.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.72,0:08:30.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,门襟纽扣就位
Dialogue: 1,0:08:28.72,0:08:30.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The closing button is positioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.92,0:08:41.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器用于制作固定腰带的裤袢
Dialogue: 1,0:08:37.92,0:08:41.12,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine is used to make the loops which will hold the belt in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.30,0:08:46.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,裤袢同样用棉线缝制
Dialogue: 1,0:08:44.30,0:08:46.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The loops are sewn, again with cotton thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.08,0:09:01.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一阶段，他们拼合牛仔裤的各部件
Dialogue: 1,0:08:58.08,0:09:01.28,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, they assemble the different pieces of the jeans.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.08,0:09:04.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,操作员在裆部拼接两片牛仔布
Dialogue: 1,0:09:02.08,0:09:04.96,Original,,0,0,0,,This operator joins the 2 pieces of denim at the crotch,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.76,0:09:10.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后缝合
Dialogue: 1,0:09:09.76,0:09:10.64,Original,,0,0,0,,then sews them together.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.40,0:09:18.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着缝制裤腿外侧
Dialogue: 1,0:09:16.40,0:09:18.48,Original,,0,0,0,,They then sew the exterior of the leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.68,0:09:22.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,用拷边机平缝
Dialogue: 1,0:09:19.68,0:09:22.32,Original,,0,0,0,,This sewing is done flat with an overcaster,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.56,0:09:24.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,同时裁去多余布料
Dialogue: 1,0:09:22.56,0:09:24.64,Original,,0,0,0,,which cuts away any excess material.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.88,0:09:30.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器安装拉链
Dialogue: 1,0:09:28.88,0:09:30.56,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine installs the zip.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.68,0:09:54.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后一道缝制工序是安装裤腰，即一条布带
Dialogue: 1,0:09:49.68,0:09:54.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The final sewing step consists of installing the jeans belt, a strip of fabric.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.00,0:10:02.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这道工序只需几秒钟
Dialogue: 1,0:10:00.00,0:10:02.24,Original,,0,0,0,,This operation requires only a few seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.84,0:10:14.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,牛仔裤是反面缝制的
Dialogue: 1,0:10:11.84,0:10:14.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The jeans were made up on the reverse side,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.24,0:10:17.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这样穿时所有线迹都藏在里面
Dialogue: 1,0:10:14.24,0:10:17.28,Original,,0,0,0,,so that all stitches would be inside when the jeans are worn.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.08,0:10:21.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后用这台翻裤机
Dialogue: 1,0:10:18.08,0:10:21.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The trouser is then turned right side out with this
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.52,0:10:24.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,借助强力吸力把裤子翻正
Dialogue: 1,0:10:21.52,0:10:24.16,Original,,0,0,0,,turner, which uses a powerful suction action.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.32,0:10:33.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,剩下的就是蒸汽熨烫牛仔裤，消除褶皱
Dialogue: 1,0:10:29.32,0:10:33.68,Original,,0,0,0,,All that now remains is to steam press the jeans to eliminate any pleats.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.32,0:10:38.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家公司每天生产 1500 条牛仔裤
Dialogue: 1,0:10:34.32,0:10:38.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This company makes 1,500 pairs of jeans every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.28,0:10:42.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,每条需耗时 12 分 50 秒的工时
Dialogue: 1,0:10:39.28,0:10:42.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Each pair will have taken 12 minutes and 50 seconds of work,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.64,0:10:46.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,用料约 1.2 米
Dialogue: 1,0:10:42.64,0:10:46.08,Original,,0,0,0,,and will have required around 1.2 meters of fabric.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.52,0:10:56.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来请看《造物小百科》：电脑
Dialogue: 1,0:10:53.52,0:10:56.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up in how it's made: computers.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.64,0:10:58.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,30 年前，没人知道这是什么
Dialogue: 1,0:10:56.64,0:10:58.88,Original,,0,0,0,,30 years ago, nobody would have known what this was.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.44,0:11:01.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今，我们已离不开它
Dialogue: 1,0:10:59.44,0:11:01.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Today, we couldn't live without one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.88,0:11:03.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有平板玻璃
Dialogue: 1,0:11:02.88,0:11:03.84,Original,,0,0,0,,And plate glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.08,0:11:05.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,它的历史超过 4000 年
Dialogue: 1,0:11:04.08,0:11:05.92,Original,,0,0,0,,It's been around for over 4,000 years,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.40,0:11:09.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,但自罗马时代以来，其制造工艺几乎没变
Dialogue: 1,0:11:06.40,0:11:09.76,Original,,0,0,0,,but its construction has remained pretty much the same since the time of the Romans.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.96,0:11:11.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,广告之后见
Dialogue: 1,0:11:10.96,0:11:11.68,Original,,0,0,0,,See you after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.36,0:11:20.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:19.36,0:11:20.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.28,0:11:22.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后我们将介绍平板玻璃
Dialogue: 1,0:11:21.28,0:11:22.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Later we look at plate glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.12,0:11:26.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,其制造工艺自罗马时代以来几乎没变
Dialogue: 1,0:11:23.12,0:11:26.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Its construction has remained pretty much the same since the time of the Romans.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.48,0:11:31.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先，就在 30 年前
Dialogue: 1,0:11:28.48,0:11:31.68,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, just 30 years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.84,0:11:34.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,没人能说出这件东西是什么
Dialogue: 1,0:11:31.84,0:11:34.00,Original,,0,0,0,,nobody could have told you what this object was,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.40,0:11:36.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,更别说它能带来的种种神奇功能
Dialogue: 1,0:11:34.40,0:11:36.72,Original,,0,0,0,,let alone the kind of wonders you could work with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.40,0:11:42.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,时代变了，如今很难想象有哪个现代家庭或
Dialogue: 1,0:11:38.40,0:11:42.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Times have changed, and today it's hard to imagine a single modern home or
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.56,0:11:45.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,办公室没有至少一台这种革命性设备
Dialogue: 1,0:11:42.56,0:11:45.60,Original,,0,0,0,,office without at least one of these revolutionary devices.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.24,0:11:53.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,组装一台电脑约需 90 分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:11:51.24,0:11:53.84,Original,,0,0,0,,It takes about 90 minutes to assemble a computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.60,0:11:57.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先安装硬盘驱动器
Dialogue: 1,0:11:55.60,0:11:57.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The hard disk drive is first.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.24,0:12:00.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,读写头负责读取信息
Dialogue: 1,0:11:58.24,0:12:00.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The reading head reads the information.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.96,0:12:02.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是一件极其精密的装置
Dialogue: 1,0:12:00.96,0:12:02.96,Original,,0,0,0,,An extremely precise piece of kit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.44,0:12:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,读写头与硬盘之间的间隙细如发丝
Dialogue: 1,0:12:03.44,0:12:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The space between it and the hard disk is as thin as a hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.68,0:12:12.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,硬盘被安装到机箱内的预定位置
Dialogue: 1,0:12:09.68,0:12:12.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The hard disk is installed in its position within the computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.68,0:12:18.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有两个保存信息的部件：
Dialogue: 1,0:12:15.68,0:12:18.40,Original,,0,0,0,,There are 2 other units which safeguard information:
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.88,0:12:21.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,可移动磁盘读取器和光盘驱动器
Dialogue: 1,0:12:18.88,0:12:21.60,Original,,0,0,0,,the removable disc reader and the CD-ROM drive,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.92,0:12:26.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,用于读取和执行光盘上记录的程序
Dialogue: 1,0:12:21.92,0:12:26.00,Original,,0,0,0,,which allows for the reading and execution of programs recorded on compact discs.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.64,0:12:32.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这两个部件安装就位
Dialogue: 1,0:12:30.64,0:12:32.56,Original,,0,0,0,,These 2 units are placed into position.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.16,0:12:37.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑的主干就是主板
Dialogue: 1,0:12:34.16,0:12:37.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The spinal column of the computer is the motherboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.76,0:12:41.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑的其他元件都连接到主板上
Dialogue: 1,0:12:37.76,0:12:41.36,Original,,0,0,0,,It's to this unit that the other elements of the computer are connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.24,0:12:45.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这款散热器散发芯片组产生的热量
Dialogue: 1,0:12:42.24,0:12:45.20,Original,,0,0,0,,This cooler dissipates the heat generated by the chipset.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.32,0:12:49.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,部分声卡直接集成在主板上
Dialogue: 1,0:12:46.32,0:12:49.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Certain sound cards are integrated directly on the motherboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.56,0:12:53.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些接口依次是音频输入、
Dialogue: 1,0:12:50.56,0:12:53.60,Original,,0,0,0,,These connections in sequence are the audio input,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.08,0:12:56.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,音频输出和麦克风接口
Dialogue: 1,0:12:54.08,0:12:56.16,Original,,0,0,0,,its output, and the microphone port.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.52,0:13:00.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个固定环在运输中固定显卡
Dialogue: 1,0:12:57.52,0:13:00.64,Original,,0,0,0,,This retaining ring secures the video card during transport
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.46,0:13:04.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,而温度传感器则测量
Dialogue: 1,0:13:01.46,0:13:04.40,Original,,0,0,0,,and this thermal unit measures the temperature emitted
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.40,0:13:06.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,处理器与主板之间的温度
Dialogue: 1,0:13:04.40,0:13:06.48,Original,,0,0,0,,between the processor and the motherboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.20,0:13:13.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,处理器是整个系统的大脑
Dialogue: 1,0:13:11.20,0:13:13.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The processor is the brains of the system.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.08,0:13:18.02,Translation,,0,0,0,,它解读、计算并执行下达给它的指令
Dialogue: 1,0:13:14.08,0:13:18.02,Original,,0,0,0,,It interprets, calculates, and executes the instructions given to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.70,0:13:25.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,处理器安置在这个底座上
Dialogue: 1,0:13:23.70,0:13:25.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The processor rests on this base.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.96,0:13:31.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,处理器的散热器散发巨大热量
Dialogue: 1,0:13:28.96,0:13:31.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The processor's cooler dissipates the intense heat.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.16,0:13:35.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,其效率取决于所用材料
Dialogue: 1,0:13:32.16,0:13:35.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Its efficiency depends on the type of material used,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.20,0:13:37.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,导热材料能带来更好的散热效果
Dialogue: 1,0:13:35.20,0:13:37.52,Original,,0,0,0,,and a conducting material ensures better cooling.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.80,0:13:43.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,内存存储短期信息，断电时信息即被清除
Dialogue: 1,0:13:38.80,0:13:43.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The RAM memory stores short-term information but erases it when the current is turned off.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.88,0:13:48.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,内存的速度快于硬盘或光盘
Dialogue: 1,0:13:44.88,0:13:48.64,Original,,0,0,0,,This memory is more rapid than that of the hard disk or the CD-ROM.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.32,0:13:54.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在把所有部件装入机箱
Dialogue: 1,0:13:52.32,0:13:54.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they integrate everything in the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.72,0:13:57.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,机箱保护内部元件免受外部环境影响
Dialogue: 1,0:13:54.72,0:13:57.68,Original,,0,0,0,,It protects the internal elements from the external elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.58,0:14:02.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一阶段，把电子元件安装进机箱
Dialogue: 1,0:13:58.58,0:14:02.40,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, they install the electronic components in the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.00,0:14:09.06,Translation,,0,0,0,,机箱上的几个接口连接到主板
Dialogue: 1,0:14:06.00,0:14:09.06,Original,,0,0,0,,Several connectors of the case are connected to the motherboard
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.06,0:14:11.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,比如各种指示灯
Dialogue: 1,0:14:09.06,0:14:11.04,Original,,0,0,0,,such as various light indicators.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.36,0:14:19.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是显卡的输出接口
Dialogue: 1,0:14:17.36,0:14:19.68,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the output connection for the video card,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.84,0:14:21.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,用于连接电脑和显示器
Dialogue: 1,0:14:19.84,0:14:21.76,Original,,0,0,0,,which links the computer to the monitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.56,0:14:27.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们还能看到显卡芯片，它负责生成 2D 和 3D 图像
Dialogue: 1,0:14:22.56,0:14:27.12,Original,,0,0,0,,We also see the video chip, which creates images in 2 and 3 dimensions.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.88,0:14:30.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是显存
Dialogue: 1,0:14:28.88,0:14:30.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Here is the video memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.80,0:14:32.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,显存容量越大
Dialogue: 1,0:14:30.80,0:14:32.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The more its capacity is increased,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.72,0:14:34.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,显示器上的图像就越清晰
Dialogue: 1,0:14:32.72,0:14:34.80,Original,,0,0,0,,the clearer the image displayed on the monitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.00,0:14:38.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,显卡安装就位
Dialogue: 1,0:14:36.00,0:14:38.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The video card is placed into position.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.04,0:14:41.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,调制解调器让两台电脑能够通信
Dialogue: 1,0:14:39.04,0:14:41.68,Original,,0,0,0,,This modem allows 2 computers to communicate.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.40,0:14:47.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,其电容产生非常干净的信号, 以便实现顺畅通信
Dialogue: 1,0:14:42.40,0:14:47.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Its capacitors produce the perfectly clean phone signal to facilitate communications.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.24,0:14:50.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,调制解调器芯片的接口控制着
Dialogue: 1,0:14:48.24,0:14:50.72,Original,,0,0,0,,These modem chip connectors control information
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.72,0:14:52.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,两台电脑之间流通的信息
Dialogue: 1,0:14:50.72,0:14:52.72,Original,,0,0,0,,circulating between the 2 computers.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.80,0:14:56.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后安装传真调制解调器
Dialogue: 1,0:14:54.80,0:14:56.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The fax modem is then installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.16,0:15:03.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,电源按各部件所需电压转换电能
Dialogue: 1,0:14:58.16,0:15:03.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The power supply transforms electricity according to the voltage required by the different components.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.88,0:15:11.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,安装电脑内部线缆
Dialogue: 1,0:15:08.88,0:15:11.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The computer's interior cabling is installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.92,0:15:15.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,它让信息能在各存储介质与主板之间流通
Dialogue: 1,0:15:11.92,0:15:15.68,Original,,0,0,0,,It allows information to travel between the different media and the motherboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.20,0:15:20.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,IDE 线缆已连接到光盘驱动器上
Dialogue: 1,0:15:18.20,0:15:20.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The IDE cable is connected to the CD-ROM.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.16,0:15:42.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后的电线连接到电脑各部件
Dialogue: 1,0:15:39.16,0:15:42.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The last electrical wires are connected to the different computer components.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.94,0:16:01.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,电脑 30 个部件的组装现已完成
Dialogue: 1,0:15:57.94,0:16:01.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The assembly of 30 components of the computer is now finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.92,0:16:08.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,合上机箱前，逐台测试电脑，确认外设运转正常
Dialogue: 1,0:16:02.92,0:16:08.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Just before closing the case, they test each computer to verify the good functioning of the peripherals.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.00,0:16:11.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后合上机箱，进入包装环节
Dialogue: 1,0:16:09.00,0:16:11.24,Original,,0,0,0,,They then close up and proceed to packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.96,0:16:15.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家公司每天生产约 300 台电脑
Dialogue: 1,0:16:11.96,0:16:15.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This company produces about 300 computer units every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.44,0:16:29.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃最早出现在 4000 年前的古埃及
Dialogue: 1,0:16:24.44,0:16:29.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Glass first arrived in the time of the Egyptians, 4,000 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.76,0:16:31.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过当时并不用于建筑
Dialogue: 1,0:16:29.76,0:16:31.68,Original,,0,0,0,,It wasn't used in construction, though,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.84,0:16:34.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,而只是用来封装小物件
Dialogue: 1,0:16:31.84,0:16:34.00,Original,,0,0,0,,but merely to enclose small objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.48,0:16:36.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,到了 19 世纪末
Dialogue: 1,0:16:34.48,0:16:36.08,Original,,0,0,0,,By the end of the nineteenth century,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.24,0:16:38.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃不再只是奢侈品
Dialogue: 1,0:16:36.24,0:16:38.40,Original,,0,0,0,,glass was no longer just a luxury item,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.64,0:16:42.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,而成为一种建筑材料，如钢铁和混凝土一样常见
Dialogue: 1,0:16:38.64,0:16:42.00,Original,,0,0,0,,but became a construction material, as common as steel and concrete.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.50,0:16:51.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,平板玻璃由多种原料加少量水混合制成
Dialogue: 1,0:16:47.50,0:16:51.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Plate glass is made from several raw materials mixed with a little water.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.40,0:17:03.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些原料是硅砂、纯碱、白云石、石灰石、霞石正长岩和芒硝
Dialogue: 1,0:16:52.40,0:17:03.68,Original,,0,0,0,,These materials are silica sand, soda ash, dolomite, limestone, nepheline syenite, and salt cake.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:52.40,0:17:03.68,Annotation,,0,0,0,,霞石正长岩：玻璃原料\N芒硝：硫酸钠，玻璃助剂
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.16,0:17:15.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先把碎玻璃与原料一起倒入料斗
Dialogue: 1,0:17:10.16,0:17:15.60,Original,,0,0,0,,It begins by dumping into a hopper pieces of recycled glass together with the raw materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.40,0:17:17.38,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们将被熔化
Dialogue: 1,0:17:16.40,0:17:17.38,Original,,0,0,0,,It will be melted.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.48,0:17:22.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,混合原料连续不断地进入燃气熔窑
Dialogue: 1,0:17:18.48,0:17:22.16,Original,,0,0,0,,In a continuous stream, the mixed materials go into a gas-fed furnace.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.52,0:17:30.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,熔窑内温度高达 1500 摄氏度
Dialogue: 1,0:17:25.52,0:17:30.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Temperature inside the furnace is 1,500 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.80,0:17:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,窑内装有 1500 吨玻璃液
Dialogue: 1,0:17:30.80,0:17:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,It contains 1,500 tons of molten glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.64,0:17:42.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,在蓄热室中，空气被预热到 1000 度
Dialogue: 1,0:17:38.64,0:17:42.72,Original,,0,0,0,,In this regenerating chamber, air is preheated to 1,000 degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.72,0:17:49.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,混合原料开始熔化融合
Dialogue: 1,0:17:46.72,0:17:49.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The materials of the mix begin fusing,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.36,0:17:51.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃液被搅拌
Dialogue: 1,0:17:49.36,0:17:51.36,Original,,0,0,0,,and the molten glass is stirred up.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.20,0:17:56.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,均化器搅匀玻璃液，使其温度均匀
Dialogue: 1,0:17:53.20,0:17:56.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This homogenizer mixes the glass to equalize its temperature.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.28,0:17:59.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,数小时后即可开始浇注
Dialogue: 1,0:17:57.28,0:17:59.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Pouring will be done within several hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.92,0:18:04.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃行业把这台机器称为上压辊
Dialogue: 1,0:18:01.92,0:18:04.88,Original,,0,0,0,,In the glass industry, they call this machine the top roller.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.52,0:18:10.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃液浇注在液态锡床上，漂浮其上，柔软如太妃糖
Dialogue: 1,0:18:05.52,0:18:10.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass is poured onto a bath of liquid tin on which it floats, as soft as toffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.12,0:18:12.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃被塑形成带状
Dialogue: 1,0:18:11.12,0:18:12.40,Original,,0,0,0,,It's molded into a ribbon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.92,0:18:16.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,锡床中的所有设备都用水冷却
Dialogue: 1,0:18:13.92,0:18:16.88,Original,,0,0,0,,All equipment in the tin bath is cooled with water so
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.88,0:18:18.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,以免受热损坏
Dialogue: 1,0:18:16.88,0:18:18.24,Original,,0,0,0,,that it won't break from the heat.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.68,0:18:25.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,离开锡床时，玻璃的温度为 600 度
Dialogue: 1,0:18:21.68,0:18:25.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming out of the bath, the glass registers at 600 degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.96,0:18:28.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃还需再次冷却
Dialogue: 1,0:18:26.96,0:18:28.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass must again be cooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.38,0:18:36.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这条巨大的玻璃带宽 3.3 米
Dialogue: 1,0:18:33.38,0:18:36.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This huge ribbon of glass is 3.3 meters in width.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.84,0:18:50.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃带在辊子上缓缓前行
Dialogue: 1,0:18:47.84,0:18:50.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The ribbon of glass rolls gently on rollers,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.56,0:18:52.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,沿途逐渐冷却
Dialogue: 1,0:18:50.56,0:18:52.16,Original,,0,0,0,,gradually cooling along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.08,0:18:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃仍然柔软
Dialogue: 1,0:18:58.08,0:18:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass is still soft.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.08,0:19:02.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们看到的痕迹是上压辊留下的压痕
Dialogue: 1,0:19:00.08,0:19:02.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The marks we see are imprints made by the top roller.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.92,0:19:08.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃必须厚度均匀
Dialogue: 1,0:19:05.92,0:19:08.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass must have a uniform thickness.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.88,0:19:12.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,激光扫描仪测厚精度可达 0.01 毫米
Dialogue: 1,0:19:08.88,0:19:12.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This laser scanner measures its thickness to within 0.01 millimeter.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.24,0:19:16.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃现在开始变硬
Dialogue: 1,0:19:14.24,0:19:16.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass is now becoming hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.72,0:19:18.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是切割阶段
Dialogue: 1,0:19:16.72,0:19:18.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Next comes the cutting stage.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.20,0:19:24.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,超硬的碳化钨辊在玻璃上划出纵向划痕，之后才能切割
Dialogue: 1,0:19:19.20,0:19:24.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This ultra-hard tungsten carbide roller makes a longitudinal score before the glass can be cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.92,0:19:28.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着进行横向划痕
Dialogue: 1,0:19:25.92,0:19:28.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they proceed with the transverse scoring.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.28,0:19:36.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃很容易被掰开
Dialogue: 1,0:19:35.28,0:19:36.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass separates easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.60,0:19:43.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃条被分离开，沿传送带继续前行
Dialogue: 1,0:19:39.60,0:19:43.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass strips are separated and continue along the conveyor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.28,0:19:58.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,辊式掰断机切掉玻璃板的边缘
Dialogue: 1,0:19:55.28,0:19:58.00,Original,,0,0,0,,These roller breakers cut the edges of the glass sheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.80,0:20:07.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,边角料落入地面滑道，日后将被回收
Dialogue: 1,0:20:02.80,0:20:07.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Leftover pieces fall to the ground and into a chute; they will later be recycled.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.32,0:20:16.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,包胶辊把玻璃板送往检验车间
Dialogue: 1,0:20:12.32,0:20:16.32,Original,,0,0,0,,These rubber-covered rollers convey the glass sheets to the inspection department.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.44,0:20:20.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃板到达检验区时
Dialogue: 1,0:20:19.44,0:20:20.88,Original,,0,0,0,,When they arrive for inspection,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.20,0:20:26.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些巨大的玻璃板被小心搬运并立放
Dialogue: 1,0:20:21.20,0:20:26.40,Original,,0,0,0,,these immense glass sheets are handled with great care and are positioned upright.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.16,0:20:41.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,用荧光灯检查玻璃是否有瑕疵
Dialogue: 1,0:20:38.16,0:20:41.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The glass is inspected for faults with fluorescent lamps.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.04,0:20:49.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,检验合格后，玻璃板逐块搬运并竖放储存
Dialogue: 1,0:20:45.04,0:20:49.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Once inspected, the glass sheets are handled one at a time and stored vertically.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.80,0:21:03.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,生产这批玻璃耗时数天
Dialogue: 1,0:21:00.80,0:21:03.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Making the glass took several days of work.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.00,0:21:07.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,高温熔融把固体原料变成
Dialogue: 1,0:21:04.00,0:21:07.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Heat fusion has transformed solid ingredients into
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.20,0:21:10.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,透明的玻璃，如今已可交付
Dialogue: 1,0:21:07.20,0:21:10.80,Original,,0,0,0,,transparent glass, and now it's ready for delivery.
